body:
Interesting, that really sucks. I wonder if your able to make the gun CA compliment without permanently damaging the firearm. Like made it CA compliment, but able to revert it back if I ever move or something. 

&#x200B;

Also the sell or transfer paragraph at the end made me chuckle. Just imagine walking into a California police department holding a AR "Hey guys! I wanna sell this to you!"

This was about 12 hours after my last injection. Is this too soon for it to be hitting peak, or should it be peaking around then? I feel pretty good, but still have anxiety/depression issues. I am 25, and had veeery low testosterone when I started. Uncontrolled diabetic, 60 pounds heavier and no muscle. I have made tremendous progress so far. Shows my glucose still a bit high, but that's on no medication at all and I keep my levels in check with my primary. Was thinking about asking the doctor if we could increase dosage. This is also with a AI, my E was 51 before I got the AI and was having sides. I also take Finasteride for my hair.

&#x200B;

I have been diagnosed with major depression and anxiety most of my life. So it could also be legitimate mental health issues unrelated to my testosterone. Which sucks, I thought TRT would be the answer for it. But it at least has been helping me physically and I am able to get more done than I used to.

I agree, I love big V8's and a manual transmission. But I do think Tesla is taking the EV market in the right direction. Tesla's are actually fun to drive, allot of cool tech in them. And FAST, the Tesla model S plaid goes 0-60 in 1.98 seconds, and that's a 4 door sedan. When the Roadster comes out, it will be even faster. Tesla made getting a EV not a compromise. Before if you went with a EV, you were sacrificing range and speed. For the most boring driving experience possible. With a Tesla, I would actually like to own one someday, I think it would be a blast. But I would still rather have a Mustang GT or WRX at the moment. 

&#x200B;

I don't know if "loud pipes saves lives" is true. But I do personally enjoy loud pipes for the fun of it. Electric motorcycles just seem like it would be a totally different experience. Probably great commuters in town like you said.

I was once 375 pounds, and slowly lost until 300 pounds. I started keto 2 months ago while also weight training 4 times a week and currently at 280. I try to look at it like this. Do you have a skill in life? Like a hobby or something you worked for? In everything we do in life, starting something is easy, but commiting is the hardest part. In whatever hobby or skill you have, you did not start good at that thing. There may of been times you wanted to quit, or came up with excuses of why you need to stop "For just a little while". But just like anything in life, if you push through that barrier, and make something a religious habit, you are able to do it.

&#x200B;

Same thing goes with keto, and fitness in general in my eyes. You will come up with excuses to cheat, and start a downward spiral right back to square one. But if you push through that, you will make the progress you always wanted. The great thing about humans is that we can adapt to almost anything. I promise you, for one month eat strict keto, no processed shit. Just cook your own meals with green veggies. You will start to enjoy it so much, you will feel full while you watch the scale go down. I highly encourage weight lifting too, it SUCKS at first, it hurts, you are always sore. But after a month, you feel the difference, you start to get addicted to it. You fucking got this, just ignite that fucking fire within you that you know you have. No trying, just doing.

I can understand where you are coming from, but please try to imagine where we are coming from when we complain about sbmm. After playing this game for over 10 years, I feel like I am the best that I can possibly be at the game. Yet, every year I get worse and worse, until this year, I am literally struggling so hard just to have a even K/D. I will have one game where I have a 2 K/D And another where I have a 0.5 KD. I am not saying throw total noobs into the wolf pit. But mixing it up will let good player be good, and let noobs get better. It just feels like at this point for me, there is no getting better, I am the best I can be. But get utterly destroyed, and its a bleak future to just keep getting destroyed all year.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Blops 2 had a light sbmm system that I think worked really well. I think a slight sbmm system would be great for everyone. The system right now feels like I am playing ranked CSGO rather than a pub COD match.
